## Tighten Databricks Apps file sync (keep Help Center)

Context: The last DAB sync uploaded 702 files. `.databricksignore` is not
applied by the CLI — only `.gitignore` plus `databricks.yml` `sync.exclude`.
Repo meta (`.github/`, `.planning/`, `ci/`, `licenses/`, changelogs, DAB YAML)
was still shipped. A bare `README.md` exclude also dropped `docs/README.md`,
so Help Center Overview 404'd.

Changes:

1. databricks.yml
   Expand `sync.exclude` for non-runtime folders; keep both README files
   because CLI 0.298 applies slash-anchored excludes recursively; document that
   `src/mcp-server/` and `src/jobs/` must stay in the shared files tree.
   Keep both `app.yaml.template` files because this CLI applies even an
   anchored root-template exclude recursively, while deploy verification
   requires the MCP template.
2. .databricksignore
   Align with `sync.exclude` as a human/test mirror (CLI does not read it).
3. src/api/routers/internal/help.py
   Point the missing-docs boot warning at `sync.exclude`.
4. tests/units/api/test_help_api.py
   Contract: no recursive README/template excludes, extra non-runtime
   excludes, and MCP/jobs kept.
5. tests/e2e/conftest.py
   Note the Overview 404 is fixed after the next deploy.
6. docs/deployment.md
   Document the real sync rules and the Help Center allow-list.
7. docs/dab-reference.md
   Same File Sync policy, shorter form.

